 preceding books, Tertullian supports his argument with profound reasoning, and many happy illustrations of Holy Scripture"}]},{"work":"anf02","title":"Ante-Nicene Fathers, Volume 2: Fathers of the Second Century","count":1,"chapters":[{"chapter":"ANFIII.8","count":1,"book":"Book Third.—Similitudes","title":"Similitude Eighth. The Sins of the Elect and of the Penitent are of Many Kinds, But All Will Be Rewarded According to the Measure of Their Repentance and Good Works"}]},{"work":"broadus1870","title":"A Treatise on the Preparation and Delivery of Sermons","count":1,"chapters":[{"chapter":"Broadus.3","count":1,"book":"Broadus","title":"SUBJECTS — CLASSIFIED"}]},{"work":"quran","title":"The Meaning of the Glorious Koran","count":1,"chapters":[{"chapter":"Quran.97","count":1,"book":"Q.","title":"Al-Qadr — The Power, Fate"}]}]}
